# Error pages + validation

Operators, not engineers. Status pages + field errors stay plain English.

## Full-page errors (400s / 500s only)

No 2xx/3xx pages. Layout: one large `<h1>`, `max-w-3xl`, left, `<p>` body. No breadcrumbs (`data-error-page`). No red text. No HTTP codes in UI (`404`, `500`, `Bad Request`). No humour (`Oops`). No blame. No vague “technical difficulties” / “maintenance” / “improvements”.

`<title>`: `{H1} – Content Studio`.

Always say next step. **Back** (history) and **Home** `/`. Docs `/documentation`.

| Case | H1 | Body |
|---|---|---|
| Missing URL | `Page not found` | Typed address: check it. Pasted: copy the whole address. Still wrong: home or docs. |
| Unexpected failure | `Sorry, there is a problem with the service` | Try again later. Work is saved. Docs if they need help now. |
| Service closed | `Sorry, the service is unavailable` | When it returns (or “later”). Whether work is saved. Other way to finish. |

Views: `NotFoundPageView`, `ServiceProblemPageView`, `ErrorPageView`.

## Validation + inline errors

Human line first. What to do, not what broke. Developer / provider / Zod JSON / stack / HTTP codes: collapsed `ErrorDetails` (`Technical details`).

- Fields: `FieldError` (destructive). Zod `customError` in `configureZodErrors` — never default “Too small: expected…”.
- Form / section / query: `InlineErrorView` or `ErrorCard` `message` + `details`.
- Persist raw in DB if needed. Present at UI via `presentError`.
